<<~ ahu #/head>>

! The persona-KEL ~ continuity rides the log, never the key

A persona's identifier is a stable PREFIX (a KERI autonomic-identifier / AID) that the operational signing key
rotates BENEATH. Reading-B recovery rotates the op-key rather than resurrecting it, so continuity CANNOT ride
the op-key — it rides this key-event-log. The module lifts the charter's proven epoch-chain machinery DOWN to
persona scale: it invents nothing structural, it re-sites what stands.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-invariant>>

!! The invariant ~ prefix fixed, head authoritative, old key superseded

# ''The identifier PREFIX stays FIXED'' — a content-address over the inception op-key plus the pre-committed
recovery-set digest, unchanged across every rotation (`personaPrefixOf`). Binding the recovery digest INTO
the prefix walls off a swap: no attacker incepts a DIFFERENT recovery set under the same identifier.
# ''Each event SEATS one operational key; the LATEST head carries the authoritative key.'' A rotation ADVANCES
the head, hash-linked onto its predecessor.
# ''The old op-key SUPERSEDES, never revives'' — eviction runs forward-only. A thief of today's op-key learns
nothing of the recovery future.

Every event content-addresses by `eventCid` over an authority CORE, and the guardian rotation-signatures sign
the SAME bytes — the revealed roster/threshold ride OUTSIDE, verified against the bound `recoverySetHash`, so
re-carrying an event never re-signs it (the sig-outside pattern). A single bit-flip yields a different cid, so
the hash-link the next event binds is tamper-evident.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/armed-inception>>

!! Armed inception + the rolling recovery commitment

Inception (seq 0, no predecessor) seats the founding op-key self-authorized — exactly as today's founder edge
self-signs. It commits only the recovery DIGEST (`recoverySetHash`), never the roster: the KERI pre-rotation
reveal happens at the ROTATION, never before, so a compromise of the operational PRESENT cannot forge the
recovery FUTURE. The inception is ''armed'' — it carries a `nextRecoverySetHash`, the rolling commitment that
authorizes the NEXT rotation, seated equal to the genesis digest at inception and grafted per event thereafter.

''Fork-B — threshold-attest'' (identity-classes#the-two-forks): inception pre-commits the k-of-n DIGEST of the
guardians' recovery PUBLIC keys (`sealKeySetHash`); a rotation carries k guardian SIGNATURES over the event
bytes, verified against that pre-commit. ''NOTHING reconstructs'' — no secret ever assembles. The recovery
authority signs ONLY rotations, never content.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-contest>>

!! The provisional / veto contest ~ liveness proposes, the standing hand disposes

A recovery rotation may land ''provisional'' — a rotation NOT yet hardened, conferring kapae-reversible
authority only. An observer hardens it by its own silence-across-K-local-epochs policy (passed as a verdict,
never computed from a clock); NOT accepting is the resting state, so a provisional head confers nothing by
default and the prior key stays head until the observer accepts.

The standing op-key's ''veto'' kills a provisional at any causal distance: one signature by the standing
holder — no quorum, because the holder's own hand IS the whole authority the contest exists to protect. A veto
COMPETES at the contested seq, links the same predecessor, and the chain continues FROM the veto; the
provisional and every descendant fall.

''The contest folds STRUCTURALLY.'' `foldPersonaContests` collapses the competing events into ONE linear
lineage — at each seq a verified veto naming a present provisional wins, the provisional and its descendants
drop. The veto's signature verifies in `verifyPersonaKelFull`, and a gate walking full REFUSES a chain whose
veto does not verify: a halt, never a silent pick.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-board>>

!! The board ~ an additive per-Nexus CRDT, fail-closed end to end

The DOC face of the persona-KEL extracts events from a per-Nexus KEL BOARD — one deterministic `LarDoc`
holding EVERY persona's log keyed by `{prefix}/{seq}`. One board per Nexus federates once and every island
member walks the same identifier→head mapping "as of my last sync" — no global lookup, no global now.

# ''Keying by `{prefix}/{seq}` makes the board ADDITIVE.'' A rotation accretes a new seq under a distinct key,
so a concurrent write never overwrites a standing event in place; the FOLD decides the head, never the write.
# ''Contest-aware keying'' suffixes the cid where a provisional and its veto compete at one seq, so a
last-writer-wins merge cannot adjudicate a contest by accident — both survive and `foldPersonaContests` picks.
# ''Extraction is PERMISSIVE, trust is downstream.'' A torn / foreign / non-KEL tiddler is SKIPPED, never
guessed; a malformed event that slips extraction dies at `verifyPersonaKel`.
# ''FAIL CLOSED.'' An absent or empty board surfaces NO chains, a prefix resolves to a null head, and the
Binding-Gate walk denies. A not-yet-synced reader surfaces a shorter chain or none, and the pin-move fails
closed on it.

The gate-walk (`verifyEdgeAgainstPersonaKel`) walks the KEL to its current authoritative op-key, then verifies
a device-delegation edge against THAT head — the pin moves from a raw op-key to the identifier's live head. A
rotated key still verifies via a fresh edge; an edge signed by a superseded op-key rejects.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/frozen-for-alpha>>

!! Frozen for alpha ~ the primitives the sibling grammar builds on

The persona-KEL ''freezes after the provisional/veto change'' — its bytes stop moving, and the handle-KEL is
built on the frozen primitives (identity-classes). The freeze is what lets a SIBLING grammar reuse the shape
by structure rather than chase a moving target: the armed inception, the rolling commitment, the content
-addressed cid, the sig-outside pattern all stand fixed. TRUE k-of-n graft governance and the Binding-Gate
wiring ride DECLARED above the freeze, not folded into it.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/duplicity-dual>>

!! Duplicity-detection ~ the dual of a registry

A registry catches a cheat by compiling a place that records everyone; this stack refuses that place
(registry-filter). The persona-KEL catches the same cheat by the DUAL move — ''duplicity is algorithmically
detectable'' (wax-stamp): two signed inconsistent events at one sequence stand as an equivocation any replica
spots locally, and the contest-aware board keeps both so the fold can see the fork rather than let a merge
hide it. The board diffuses chains their subjects author (carriage, per the filter's own construction); the
DAY any gate reads board-presence as truth-of-now it crosses into registry. Safety turns on the CHAIN — the
fold, the quorum, the veto — never on the board's liveness.

<<~/ahu>>

